################################################################################
# ENTA - public repository
#
# DENY BY DEFAULT. Everything is ignored unless a rule below explicitly
# un-ignores it. The ENTA working folder holds confidential microdata, API
# tokens, internal notes and pipeline output alongside the code, so an
# allow-list is the only structure that keeps a newly created file from
# reaching the public repo by accident. When you add a file that belongs in
# the repo, add it here too - "git add" alone will not pick it up.
#
# The repository holds everything needed to reproduce ENTA except the
# licensed microdata (EU-SILC, LFS, HBS, EUROMOD, Konsumerhebung): the code,
# the input files that cannot be downloaded from Eurostat, and the manual.
# Output - age profiles, aggregates, final data - is not stored; the code
# rebuilds it, and the published data are on Zenodo.
################################################################################

# 1. Ignore everything ...
*

# 2. ... but still descend into directories, so the rules below can match.
!*/


################################################################################
# 3. Code
################################################################################

!.gitignore
!/README.md
!/LICENSE
!/CITATION.cff

# Setup: path globals, the download switch, and the programs (adjust*,
# gensex) that nearly every other file calls. Run this first.
!ENTA_setup.do

# Final compilation
!ENTA_compilation1_esa.do
!ENTA_compilation2_nta.do
!ENTA_compilation3_parquet.R

# Input-data preparation, age profiles, aggregates
!ENTA_input_data/*.do
!ENTA_ageprofiles/*.do
!ENTA_aggregates/*.do

# Control of the published output: the checks, the ledger they read, and
# their findings (CSV only; rewritten by every run). No microdata needed.
# benchmarks/: the public data of the external comparisons (4a-4c); the two
# method PDFs there are third-party documents and stay out.
!ENTA_output_control/*.do
!ENTA_output_control/ledger.csv
!ENTA_output_control/README.md
!ENTA_output_control/results/*.csv
!ENTA_output_control/results/external/*.csv
!ENTA_output_control/benchmarks/*.csv
!ENTA_output_control/benchmarks/*.dta

# Checks that need the microdata, run by hand (manual chapter 5).
!ENTA_microdata_checks/*.do
!ENTA_microdata_checks/README.md


################################################################################
# 4. Input data: the Eurostat tables as downloaded, and the files that the
#    code cannot download
################################################################################

# The Eurostat tables used for this version (Stata files under their Eurostat
# code). Eurostat revises its tables, so they are stored to make the
# published aggregates reproducible; the download switch in ENTA_setup.do
# fetches current versions instead.
!ENTA_input_data/Original_input_data/*.dta

# World Bank CPI (manual download) and DG TAXUD tax revenue by function
!ENTA_input_data/Original_input_data/CPI_world_bank.xls
!ENTA_input_data/Original_input_data/taxud_tax_ec_func_en.csv
# DG TAXUD national tax lists and PIT split (manual download; Suppl_tax_list.do)
!ENTA_input_data/Original_input_data/National_tax_list_2026.xlsx

# UN World Population Prospects (population_UN.dta, covered by the rule
# above) - the API needs a personal token, which is never shared (section 6)

# Public health profile from the 2018 Ageing Report (CGH_AWG.dta). Its
# source is published too: the Ageing Report charts digitised with
# WebPlotDigitizer (zip), the script that cleans them and the resulting rates
# (csv). The code that turns the rates into CGH_AWG is not published.
!ENTA_input_data/ENTA_input_datasets/CGH_AWG.dta
!ENTA_input_data/Original_input_data/Health_exp_ageing_report.csv
!ENTA_input_data/Original_input_data/Health_exp_ageing_report_WebPlotDigitizerDaten.zip
!ENTA_input_data/Original_input_data/Health_exp_ageing_report_data_cleaning.R

# Tax shares derived from EUROMOD (country x year aggregates, no microdata)
!ENTA_input_data/ENTA_input_datasets/taxr.dta
!ENTA_input_data/ENTA_input_datasets/inctax_nonempl_decomp.dta


################################################################################
# 5. Manual and codebook - the PDFs only, not their LaTeX sources
################################################################################

!2026_ENTA_Manual_V_2_0_0/Manual.pdf
!2026_ENTA_Manual_V_2_0_0/Codebook.pdf


################################################################################
# 6. Never share - restated, so the intent survives any edit above
#
# Deny-by-default already excludes all of this. These rules only name what
# must never be un-ignored. Do NOT add a folder here that section 3-5 opens
# (e.g. "ENTA_input_data/Original_input_data/"): git cannot re-include a file
# from an excluded folder, so the allow rules above would silently stop
# working.
################################################################################

# Machine-specific setup
ENTA_setup_TU.do

# Credentials
token_population_data.txt
**/un_api_token.txt

# Output (rebuilt by the code, published on Zenodo). Contents only, not the
# folders: each keeps its README.md so a fresh clone has the folder, and git
# cannot re-include a file from an excluded folder.
ENTA_output_data/*
!ENTA_output_data/README.md
ENTA_ageprofiles/ageprofiles/*
!ENTA_ageprofiles/ageprofiles/README.md
ENTA_aggregates/*.dta

# Internal working notes
CLAUDE.md
ENTA_bug_report.txt
ENTA_todo.txt
ENTA_todo_next_version.txt
ENTA_next_session.md
TX_residual_review.md

# Editor / OS byproducts
.claude/
desktop.ini
*.log
*.stswp
~*.stswp
